branch: feature/optics-outside-routes-adopt
worktree: ../okay-wt-adopt

why: the last two hand-written routes in the tree, and the entry that
  has been open since stage 1 closes with them. Both compare the WHOLE
  request target, so both 404 on a query string — the class live since
  e9901797 stopped Jetty dropping it:
    okay-admin   POST /admin/replay
    okay-demo    GET  /whoami   (TwoNode.leaderGated)

  Surveyed and DELIBERATELY LEFT ALONE, with reasons, so nobody
  converts them later by pattern-matching on shape:
    okay-acme   already correct — it has its own `path(url)` that cuts
                the query before comparing, the only module that did.
    okay-security/McpAuth  `startsWith("/.well-known/oauth-protected-
                resource")` looks like the /person → /personal
                sloppiness and is not: RFC 9728 allows the resource's
                path as a suffix, so the prefix is probably deliberate.
                Converting it would break spec compliance.

what: both become Routers. TwoNode's `leaderGated` keeps its own
  `isDefinedAt`/`apply` wrapper, which is what applies the 503 to a
  POST from a follower — only the `whoami` half becomes a table.

next: failing tests, the conversions, docs
